WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:05.560
I'm going to talk to you about 10 things you
can do to increase the value of your business.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.370
But before I do that, let me kind of put things
in perspective so you kind of have an idea

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:14.320
why this mindset of value, profit, conversations
you always hear about.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.500
So many people run a business and by the time
the year end comes with taxes, any profit

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.601
that the company makes, they like to take
it out, pay taxes on it, and put it in their

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:24.601
own checking account, right?

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:28.560
Because it's my profit, it's my business,
it's my this, it's my that.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.920
And then there are those that say, man, this
is what I need to live off of, but let's let

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:33.920
it ride.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:34.920
Let it ride.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.920
Let's grow it.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:36.920
Let's let it ride.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.920
Let's invest.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:38.920
Let's let it ride.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.679
What is the difference between the two and
why does some do one over the other?

00:00:40.679 --> 00:00:41.679
Here's the difference.

00:00:41.679 --> 00:00:42.820
Profit, value.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:45.340
Short term, long term.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:49.730
Working in the business to make money now,
working on the business to increase value

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:50.809
later.

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:52.969
Now, later.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:57.090
Instant gratification, delayed gratification.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:01.399
More like a sales mentality [profit], more
like a CEO mentality [value].

00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:05.000
Independent contractor mentality [profit],
business owner mentality [value].

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.369
So this is something you see a lot in business.

00:01:07.369 --> 00:01:11.280
So you may be wondering yourself and say,
"Pat, I get it, but I want to increase the

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.880
value of my business.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.460
What should I do to increase the value of
my business?"

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.340
I got ten keys for you.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:24.799
#1, if the business is based on a technology
that you own that a person, a company may

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:29.640
have interest in wanting to buy your company,
that that technology can be used in their

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.740
entire spectrum of business that they're doing,
that increases the value of the business,

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.189
especially if you own the technology.

00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:41.320
If your business is ran on technology and
systems and CRMs and back office, all these

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:46.759
things that make things go faster, where,
you know, you'll typically need 200 employees

00:01:46.759 --> 00:01:51.490
to do this, but because you have the technology
you only need 45 employees to do this, people

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:54.710
who want to buy a company like that and that
increases the value of the company.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.289
#2, focus.

00:01:56.289 --> 00:01:59.909
Your focus into what you're doing, there was
once a book written I read I think it's called

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:05.280
Built to Sell, Built to Sell is a book, a
phenomenal book, I think every entrepreneur

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.930
running a business ought to read the book
Built to Sell because what the book tells

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:13.590
you is not to focus on selling your business.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:15.530
Focus on getting focused with your business.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.000
So what is the product?

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.000
What do you do?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.330
Hey, I'm trying to do this.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:20.390
I'm trying to do this.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.790
We do this, we do this.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.980
So many different things that you do where
to increase the value of your business, why

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:30.110
don't you focus on one, two or three things
that you do, but increase your attention on

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.260
those things.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.459
It increases the value of your business.

00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:37.630
I understand how sometimes it can be tempting
to say, but Pat, if we do more, the value

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.630
goes higher.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.630
It does not.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.470
The more focused you are, the more you increase
the value of your business.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:46.700
#3, a business that's ran on systems, not
just you, increases value.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:52.400
If I can come into your company and I walk
through, and I say, What did she just say

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.460
on the phone call right now?

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.160
Oh, she said this, this, this, this.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.150
Do you have it on a sheet of paper?

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.680
Uh, no, we just taught her.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.680
What if a new person comes in.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:00.680
How do they learn?

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.459
Oh, they just sit right next to her.

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:03.459
Is that typed out?

00:03:03.459 --> 00:03:04.459
No.

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:05.459
That's systems.

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:06.459
You don't have it.

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:07.459
You need to.

00:03:07.459 --> 00:03:08.459
. . okay, we'll type it out.

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:11.360
If I come in and you have a new employee,
what are the steps when a new employee comes

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:12.360
in?

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.360
Step number one, two, three, four, five, six.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.360
You don't have that?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.360
You need that.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.829
It the person buys this product, what's their
next step?

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:17.829
What do you do next?

00:03:17.829 --> 00:03:18.829
What do you do follow up?

00:03:18.829 --> 00:03:19.829
We don't have that.

00:03:19.829 --> 00:03:20.829
We don't have that written out.

00:03:20.829 --> 00:03:21.900
These are systems and procedures.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.319
Businesses are built on systems.

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:28.170
Grow more value because it's got a life of
its own without the human being.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:32.950
Now obviously, you need a driver, but the
system takes your business value to a whole

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:33.950
different level.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:34.980
#4, Strategic partners.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.580
What are we talking about with strategic partners?

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.489
Look, strategic partners not only validate
the business, they increase the value of the

00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:41.489
business.

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:46.030
They have good things to say about you, and
when it comes down to it, they can bring complete

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.650
different aspects to your business that you
may not have yourself.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:53.040
So I think strategic partners play a very
big role in increasing the value of your business.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.599
#5 is recurring revenue.

00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:58.319
Ask yourself with the business you have right
now, what part of it recurring?

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:01.680
What do you make every single month in your
business whether you make a single sale or

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.750
not?

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:08.739
Recurring revenue produces the highest multiples
that if somebody buys this book it's got the

00:04:08.739 --> 00:04:09.909
highest multiples.

00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:11.670
Next, is supporting cast.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.159
Operations and supporting cast.

00:04:14.159 --> 00:04:15.161
Who is around you?

00:04:15.161 --> 00:04:16.730
Who's running the company?

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:21.090
This is the part where somebody who's driven
on profits, they don't invest in the people.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.340
So the value doesn't increase.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.600
I remember many years ago I was running a
sales office, and there were these two guys

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.780
who were my competitors.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.450
And I'll never forget a call I had.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.630
It was within a week apart with each one of
them.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:38.950
And we were doing a cruise contest, something
like that I was running for a sales contest.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:42.360
And they both had bigger distribution lists
than I did.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:43.360
I had a smaller one.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.590
But by the time it was done, they only had
six people or four people they wanted to pay

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:53.600
to go to cruise because it was going to cost
them $600 or $800 and they said, no, I'm not

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.000
going to pay for them because of . . .

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.010
I said, man, you've got to invest into your
people.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:03.810
So what I did is I went and paid into it for
43 people, them and their spouse.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.600
And we went on the cruise.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.670
Those guys had two.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.480
This guy had three.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:09.570
We had 43 people there.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.650
Okay, investing into the people.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.690
The level of loyalty we got from them who
were willing to come back and wanted to learn

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:19.650
more, improve more, better the company more,
was a lot higher.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.800
That's investing into a supporting cast that
wants to be in the company.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:26.770
So the more you invest into your supporting
cast to help them get better, they're more

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:30.000
indebted to you, they're more loyal to you,
they'll stay with you longer, and the value

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.780
of the company goes higher the better supporting
cast you have.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:36.490
By the way, this also goes with your executive
team, who you bring onboard as an executive

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:41.380
team, your sales force, every single thing
that is part of the supporting cast to growing

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:42.380
the business.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:43.600
#7, data.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.880
Sometimes you see companies that buy another
company and they cut a big billion dollar

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.660
check and you say, that company's revenue
was only $50 million a year.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.380
Why did they cut a check like that?

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:58.410
Because they have access to a lot of data
that they need.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:02.060
So if you have data, data increases value
of a business.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:06.750
What type of data are you gathering yourself
and how big is it, how wide is it, how deep

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.772
is it that another person, another company
can say, this is valuable and it increases

00:06:10.772 --> 00:06:12.700
the value of your business.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.200
#8, EBITDA vs. need.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:17.220
Let me explain what EBITDA vs. need is.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:26.670
EBITDA stands for Earnings Before Income,
Taxation, Depreciation, and Amortization.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:27.670
That's what EBITDA stands for, right?

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:33.340
So a lot of times you'll hear a company say,
well, why would we buy your company because

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:38.000
your EBITDA is so low and you know, if we
do the multiples based on your EBITDA, yes,

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.180
your top-line revenue was XYZ, but your EBITDA
is so small, you know, why would we do that?

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:44.800
Because you're solving for EBITDA.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.380
I'm not solving for EBITDA, I'm solving for
value.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.970
You're solving for profit.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.280
If I solve for profit, I stay flat.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:54.560
Because I solve for value, I've grown quarter
after quarter after quarter after quarter

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.070
as a business because I'm solving for value.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:02.830
So, the more you focus on a need, meaning,
going to your industry, whatever business

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:06.170
you're in, and find a need that exists that
no one's focused on.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.450
For us, there's a need that we have.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:12.900
Increase the need, where if somebody has an
interest in your business one day, it won't

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.440
be based on the EBITDA.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:19.090
It will be because this need will fill another
void that they have that the profits here

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:22.980
will go up to the roof because they locked
in a need here.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:28.120
Two businesses, this one [need] increases
a side that's about distribution this side

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:30.080
increases the profits.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:33.820
This profit that they make here is well worth
them paying for the company, the value of

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:37.680
the company because you're solving for a need,
not just for EBITDA, although you still need

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.170
to have profits, no company that goes out
of business, your company's worth nothing.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:44.200
You do need to have a focus here [EBITDA],
but not to the point where it's only short-term

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.950
instead of long-term.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:48.460
Next, subscribership and distribution.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.460
What is that?

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:53.410
That's an audience, you know, when you see
a company like Instagram being bought, but

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.270
they don't know how to make money, why are
they buying them?

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:56.400
It's because they have an audience.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.500
There's a distribution.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.210
So always focus on what you can do to increase
the distribution of your business, your company,

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.210
the eyeballs.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:05.870
The amount of people that are seeing it.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.180
The subscribership, the customer base.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:11.020
It has something to do with recurring revenue,
but it doesn't.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:15.590
There's somebody that's constantly coming
to you that's logging on to your website.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:23.920
Like, you know, a Huffington Post has subscribership
that people are coming to it and email subscribership,

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:27.030
anything that's listening to something that
you're offering that increases the value.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:29.970
And last but not least, stay hands on to increase
the value of your business.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:33.599
I think a lot of times people take their hands
off the business too early and they become

00:08:33.599 --> 00:08:39.129
CEOs too early instead of becoming you know,
somebody that's a businessman that at the

00:08:39.129 --> 00:08:41.750
end of the day your job is to increase the
value of the company and if you do a good

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.440
job increasing the value of the company, you're
a CEO.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.079
You're a great CEO.

00:08:46.079 --> 00:08:48.310
But don't take your hands off too early.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:56.300
A stay hands on CEO or executive or entrepreneur
knows about what's going on with technology.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:59.269
Knows about how focused the product is and
if we're getting distracted.

00:08:59.269 --> 00:09:03.100
Knows about the system, is hands on with the
strategic partners because he makes the calls.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.470
Is hands on with the recurring revenue.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:08.519
Is hands on supporting cast, is hands on with
the data that's being gathered, is hands on

00:09:08.519 --> 00:09:10.670
with the need and the EBITDA and is paying
attention.

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:13.550
Is hands on in increasing distribution and
subscribership.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:16.290
Always stay hands on to increase the value
of your business.

